## How do you do this in a single line?

Is there any way to do this in a single line?

I've tried the following but it doesn't work:

\documentclass{article}
\usepackage{tikz}
\begin{document}
\begin{tikzpicture}
\draw[step=1cm,gray,very thin] (0,0) grid (3,3);
\draw (0,0) rectangle (3,3);
\end{tikzpicture}
\end{document}


I want the grid to be in the rectangle.

## 4 Answers

You can use the even odd rule as follows:

\documentclass{article}
\usepackage{tikz}
\begin{document}
\begin{tikzpicture}
\draw[step=1cm,gray,very thin] (0,0) grid (3,3);
\draw[even odd rule] (0,0) rectangle (3,3);
\end{tikzpicture}
\end{document}


