# Are there any reliable methods to generate an untraceable IP address?

I'm trying to make a program that sends a message to an IP address, but I want to make sure that the IP address is untraceable. I know that the IP address can be spoofed, but is there any reliable way to do this? I've tried the following code, but it doesn't seem to work.

import java.net.InetAddress;
import java.net.NetworkInterface;
import java.util.Enumeration;

public class Ip {

public static void main(String[] args) throws Exception {
Enumeration<NetworkInterface> interfaces = NetworkInterface.getNetworkInterfaces();
while (interfaces.hasMoreElements()) {
NetworkInterface networkInterface = interfaces.nextElement();

if (!networkInterface.isLoopback()) {
for (Enumeration<InetAddress> inetAddresses = networkInterface.getInetAddresses(); inetAddresses.hasMoreElements(); ) {
InetAddress inetAddress = inetAddresses.nextElement();

if (!inetAddress.isLoopbackAddress()) {
System.out.println(inetAddress.getHostAddress());
}
}
}
}
}
}
